NC Digital creates professional logos and brand identities for businesses across Mid Wales. Every logo is designed by hand — no AI, no templates — and built to work at every size across every platform.

## Your brand is your first impression

Before a customer speaks to you, they've already made a judgement based on how your business looks. A professional logo signals that you're established and trustworthy. An amateurish or generic one sends the opposite message.

We work with tradespeople, service businesses, retailers, and start-ups across [Aberystwyth](/logo-design-aberystwyth/), [Newtown](/logo-design-newtown/), [Welshpool](/logo-design-welshpool/), [Llandrindod Wells](/logo-design-llandrindod-wells/), [Brecon](/logo-design-brecon/), [Machynlleth](/logo-design-machynlleth/), [Builth Wells](/logo-design-builth-wells/), [Hay-on-Wye](/logo-design-hay-on-wye/), and the wider Mid Wales area, giving them a visual identity that reflects what they actually do.

## What's included

- 5 initial logo concepts
- Revisions until you're completely happy
- Brand colour palette and typography choices
- Brand guidelines document
- All file formats: PNG, SVG, PDF, JPEG

Full details on our [logo design service](/services/logo-design/) page.

## No AI. Designed by hand.

Every logo is drawn in Adobe Illustrator — no AI-generated artwork, no stock icons. Unique to your business.

## Pair it with your website

We design and build websites alongside brand identities. If you need a new website for your Mid Wales business, see our [web design Mid Wales service](/web-design-mid-wales/) or [view our portfolio](/portfolio/).

## Frequently asked questions

**How much does logo design cost?**

Contact us for a fixed-price quote with no hidden costs.

**How long does it take?**

Most projects are completed within 5–10 working days.

**Do I own the logo?**

Yes — full ownership of all files transfers to you on completion.

**Do you work across all of Mid Wales?**

Yes — we work with businesses across [Aberystwyth](/logo-design-aberystwyth/), [Newtown](/logo-design-newtown/), [Welshpool](/logo-design-welshpool/), [Llandrindod Wells](/logo-design-llandrindod-wells/), [Brecon](/logo-design-brecon/), [Machynlleth](/logo-design-machynlleth/), [Builth Wells](/logo-design-builth-wells/), [Hay-on-Wye](/logo-design-hay-on-wye/), and anywhere else in Mid Wales.

